{%- comment -%}
  Is this scheduled_event inside the display window?

  Outputs "1" when it is, and nothing when it is not. Single source of truth: the same
  question was asked twice in lena-find-us.liquid - once to count cards for the grid
  layout, once to render them - with the arithmetic written out in full both times. A
  change to one copy made data-cards disagree with the number of cards actually drawn,
  and the symptom of that is a wrong column count, which looks like a CSS fault and is
  not one.

  Accepts: event (a scheduled_event metaobject)

  Consume it the way breadcrumbs consumes lena-category-handles, since a snippet cannot
  return a value:

    {%- capture visible -%}{%- render 'lena-event-window', event: event -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if visible == '1' -%}

  The window: from now until 14 days ahead, and an event stays up until a day after it
  ends. An event with no end date is treated as ending when it starts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign ev_window = 1209600
  assign ev_grace = -86400

  if event.start_date.value != blank
    assign ev_now = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign ev_start = event.start_date.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign ev_end = ev_start
    if event.end_date.value != blank
      assign ev_end = event.end_date.value | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    endif
    assign ev_from_now = ev_start | minus: ev_now
    assign ev_until_end = ev_end | minus: ev_now
    if ev_from_now <= ev_window and ev_until_end >= ev_grace
      echo '1'
    endif
  endif
-%}
